# Deane Auto Repairs — Shop supplies on Parts invoices

Updated 29 Aug 2026.

## Done: Consumable + Tool line categories
On Parts invoices (Repco / BNT / PartMaster Extracted Items), lines can be marked:

- **Consumable** — workshop supplies not for one vehicle (gloves, rags, WD-40, sandpaper, etc.)
- **Tool** — tools/equipment bought for the shop (not for one vehicle)

Both:
- Do **not** attach to a job / inflate Customer charged
- Count toward invoice **matched** (resolved) so `12/12 matched` when all lines are Accept / Consumable / Tool / Ignore
- Roll into invoice tracking and the list **this month** summary (by invoice date, Auckland)

## Do not
- Match shop consumables/tools onto a random job just because Smart Match suggested it
- Treat “Consumable” / “Tool” / “Shop supplies” as a supplier name; they are **line decisions**, not Repco/BNT/PartMaster
